# Vercel Speed Insights Configuration - Already Implemented

## Summary
Upon investigation, Vercel Speed Insights is **already properly installed and configured** in this project. No changes were necessary.

## Current Implementation Status

### 1. Package Installation ✅
- Package: `@vercel/speed-insights` version `2.0.0`
- Installed in: `web/package.json`
- Dependencies properly installed via `npm install`

### 2. Component Integration ✅
- Location: `web/src/app/layout.tsx`
- Import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next"`
- Usage: `<SpeedInsights />` component added to the root layout body
- Implementation matches the official Vercel documentation for Next.js 13.5+

### 3. CSP Configuration ✅
- Location: `web/next.config.ts`
- Properly configured Content Security Policy headers for Speed Insights
- Includes required origins:
  - `https://va.vercel-scripts.com` (script source)
  - `https://vitals.vercel-insights.com` (vitals endpoint)

### 4. Framework Compatibility ✅
- Project: Next.js 16.3.5 (latest)
- Using App Router architecture
- SpeedInsights correctly imported from `@vercel/speed-insights/next`

## Verification Steps Completed

1. ✅ Fetched latest documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart
2. ✅ Verified package installation (`npm ls @vercel/speed-insights`)
3. ✅ Confirmed proper import and component usage in root layout
4. ✅ Ran `npm install` to ensure dependencies are properly installed
5. ✅ Executed `npm run build` - Build successful with no errors
6. ✅ Ran `npm run lint` - No linting errors
7. ✅ Verified CSP headers include Speed Insights domains

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the exact pattern recommended in the official Vercel documentation:

```typescript
import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";

export default function RootLayout({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body>
        {children}
        <SpeedInsights />
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

## Next Steps

The Speed Insights integration is complete and ready for use. Once this application is deployed to Vercel:
1. Speed Insights will automatically activate
2. Performance metrics will be collected and visible in the Vercel dashboard
3. No additional configuration or deployment steps are required

